trator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56451, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RFMGufAGVnJNtnsH97Xqs5", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56451, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RFMGufAGVnJNtnsH97Xqs5", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58621, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017u5hzSps2bbNYUGiTJQVKB", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58921, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017u5hzSps2bbNYUGiTJQVKB", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58921, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017u5hzSps2bbNYUGiTJQVKB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64347, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1-rc, the release just before v2.3.1, was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- **First attempt:** this stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east was done. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n- **Second attempt:** I ran the rollback once more, since rolling back to a healthy version is safe to repeat. This time it finished in all regions.\n- **Now:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The first request to create it timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate incident and the on-call engineer wasn't paged twice.\n- It describes the failure, both rollback attempts, the current state and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SShrW6sRqVmiKebtHyYyRn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QLW86J8jf4zSTVJNsYse6L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QvzXWzS3pqor9ZJmccdT7b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PsYCeVqCssaXALGA7kzAu5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy release is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017crejwnMCGUNScqxjcEHEx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DffLytLjzVRVzaFe23Rtnj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FadMDpEUVwmReyV7gVcW4X", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RFMGufAGVnJNtnsH97Xqs5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. The previous deploy, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. Action: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy before v2.3.1 was released), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017u5hzSps2bbNYUGiTJQVKB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1-rc, the release just before v2.3.1, was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- **First attempt:** this stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east was done. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1.\n- **Second attempt:** I ran the rollback once more, since rolling back to a healthy version is safe to repeat. This time it finished in all regions.\n- **Now:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The first request to create it timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate incident and the on-call engineer wasn't paged twice.\n- It describes the failure, both rollback attempts, the current state and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. The release before it, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}